# Owner-gated paths. Anything not listed here merges on the agent's own say-so once checks
# pass, provided the ruleset on main requires code-owner review (AGENTS.md, "Owner checklist":
# a repo made from this template starts without that ruleset). GitHub reads this file from the
# base branch; the last matching line wins; a line with no owner un-gates its paths; an invalid
# line is skipped silently (the codeowners-guard workflow reads GitHub's error list).
# Patterns follow gitignore rules: a leading "/" anchors to the repo root; a bare name or "dir/"
# matches at any depth. Why a path is here, and when to add one: AGENTS.md.
# .github/scripts/codeowners_guard.py fails when a file that runs or loads unread is not owned.

# The gate itself, CI and the guard: workflows are code on GitHub's runners.
/.github/ @bogheorghiu

